## 2026-07-27 - US-006

Convert `pages/app.js`, `pages/create-torrent-page.js` and
`pages/preferences-page.js` to ESM.

**Interpretation:** a mechanical module-format conversion with no unit
test runner in the repo yet (US-019), so per execution rule 3 no
failing test was written first. The behavioural claims -- the
preferences page and the create-torrent page still render -- were
verified empirically against the running app instead; see Verification.

**What was implemented**

- `pages/app.js`: `require` -> `import`, `module.exports = App` ->
  `export default App`. `colors.*` became named imports
  (`grey50`, `grey600`, `redA100/200/400`). The lazy
  `require('material-ui/styles/baseThemes/lightBaseTheme')` inside
  `getModal()` is now a top-level import.
- Dropped `fn-getter` from `app.js`. The `Views` and `Modals` maps now
  hold the components directly instead of `createGetter(() =>
  require(...))` thunks, and the two call sites lost their `()`.
  Consequence: all four views and all five modals load at startup
  rather than on first use. There is no synchronous ESM import, so the
  old laziness is not expressible; the Vite bundle would include them
  all regardless. `fn-getter` stays a dependency -- `main.js` still
  uses it for `Cast`.
- `pages/create-torrent-page.js` and `pages/preferences-page.js`:
  imports and `export default` only, plus `colors.grey400` ->
  `grey400` in preferences.
- Added `src/renderer/pages/AGENTS.md` documenting the two registries
  and the material-ui import shapes.

**Files changed**

- `src/renderer/pages/app.js`
- `src/renderer/pages/create-torrent-page.js`
- `src/renderer/pages/preferences-page.js`
- `src/renderer/pages/AGENTS.md` (new)
- `specs/prd.json`, `progress.log`

**Verification**

- `npm test` (standard + depcheck) passes, exit 0.
- `npm run build` (Babel) compiles 64 files; the three outputs are
  `"use strict"` ESM-interop modules.
- `npx vite build` succeeds.
- App launched via `npx electron --no-sandbox .` with a temporary
  probe appended to `build/main/index.js` (never to source), reaching
  `init: 908.813ms`. The probe drove the renderer:
  `.header` outerHTML present (463 chars); `dispatch('preferences')`
  rendered the full preferences page (Folders / Download location /
  Watch for new .torrent files / Playback / External player / Highest
  Playback Priority / Default torrent app);
  `dispatch('showCreateTorrent', ['/tmp/wt-probe'])` on a throwaway
  2-file directory rendered "Create torrent wt-probe / 2 files, 12 B /
  Path:/tmp/wt-probe/ / SHOW ADVANCED SETTINGS... / CANCEL / CREATE
  TORRENT". No new renderer errors: the only severity-3 line is the
  pre-existing `electron.remote` /`getCurrentWindow` failure already
  recorded under US-005. `npm run build` was re-run afterwards to
  discard the probe.
- The six-step manual smoke test was **not** run -- this session is
  non-interactive. The residual risk is the interactive paths the DOM
  probe cannot reach: clicking CHANGE on a path selector (opens a real
  native dialog through `@electron/remote`) and actually completing
  CREATE TORRENT.

**Learnings for future iterations:**

- **`state.location.go` + `window.dispatch` is enough to render the
  create-torrent page non-interactively.**
  `dispatch('showCreateTorrent', ['<dir>'])` with a real directory path
  walks the folder with `fs` and lands on the page, so a throwaway
  `/tmp` directory with two files is a complete probe fixture. It only
  works from the home route -- `showCreateTorrent` bails with an error
  toast otherwise, so `dispatch('back')` first if the probe navigated
  away.
- **Two web contents means two probe runs.** The `did-finish-load`
  hook fires for the hidden webtorrent window too, where
  `document.querySelector('.header')` is null and
  `document.querySelector('.content')` throws. Expect one `no-header`
  and one script failure per run and do not read them as regressions;
  guard the probe or just tolerate the noise.
- **Grep the launch log for `PROBE` specifically.** Filtering with a
  combined pattern and `head -40` buried all 8 probe lines under ~150
  lines of `webtorrent: queueing` chatter and looked exactly like "the
  probe never ran".
